": "Georgia remains one of the closest presidential battlegrounds, with a partisan lean of roughly one point Republican and no incumbent on the ballot in 2028. The state's recent history has been volatile: Democrats have won statewide repeatedly, including Jon Ossoff's re-election to the Senate in 2026, while Republicans still hold the presidency and most other statewide offices.\n\nOssoff is the most prominent Georgia Democrat being discussed for 2028, and prediction markets have at times made him a favorite for the nomination, but he has repeatedly said he will not run. Without state polls or expert ratings, the forecast rests on fundamentals, and the race sits in a narrow tossup band with wide uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4567, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4683, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.467, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4627, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4625, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4617, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.4629, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4605, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4643, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4656, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4556, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.455, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.4633, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.4617, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.4576, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.463, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.4404, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.4642, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.4614, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.4606, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.4466, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.4645, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-1